chemistrydesk\src\pages\about.astro:
    5  <BaseLayout 
    6:   title="About Chemistrycal | Research-Grade Benchtop Computational Suite"
    7:   description="Learn about Chemistrycal, an open scientific utility suite developed by physical and analytical chemists to eliminate benchtop volumetric errors and provide standardized stoichiometric workflows."
    8  >

   16        <h1 style="font-size: 2.5rem; font-weight: 800; color: #0f172a; letter-spacing: -0.025em; margin: 0 0 1rem 0;">
   17:         About Chemistrycal
   18        </h1>

   29        <p>
   30:         Chemistrycal was founded and is actively maintained by <strong>Bilal Khan</strong>, a physical chemistry researcher and educator based in Hazro, District Attock, Pakistan. His research background encompasses <strong>materials chemistry, metal-organic frameworks (HKUST-1 composites), advanced oxidation processes (AOPs), and solution plasma catalytic degradation</strong>.
   31        </p>

   64        <p>
   65:         Having worked extensively across academic synthesis laboratories and practical teaching academies, the founder designed Chemistrycal to solve a persistent lab failure point: the discrepancy between theoretical textbook formulas and practical balance weighing—specifically accounting for <em>crystalline hydration water (&middot;nH₂O)</em>, manufacturer <em>assay purity percentages</em>, and <em>instrumental X-ray peak broadening</em>.
   66        </p>

   74        <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
   75:         All calculators on Chemistrycal adhere strictly to internationally recognized scientific conventions:
   76        </p>

  107        <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; color: #475569; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
  108:         Chemistrycal is registered and permanently archived in CERN's open-access repository via Zenodo. If you employ this computational suite in thesis dissertations, peer-reviewed manuscripts, or standard laboratory protocol documentation, please cite the permanent record:
  109        </p>
  110        <pre style="background: #0f172a; color: #e2e8f0; padding: 1.25rem; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.85rem; line-height: 1.6; overflow-x: auto; font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, monospace; margin: 0;">
